  "source_behavior": [
    "C10-C12 bind one original, the fixed session/request identities, qualified BOSH-only P/M literals and bounded responder/extra-item shapes. Existing C06/C08 literals retain their separate forms.",
    "Receipt authority uses the exact preceding invocation request; eventual returned mappings are checked separately. Independent ACK calls and received HTTP/generic-receipt observations still require their earlier renewal/bind/ACK authority when summary flags are cleared.",
    "The matcher binds distinct Outbound and Request ownership; initial/replay/fresh renewals, binding, response exposure, cache insertion, replay and fresh ACK eviction preserve their source callback order. Dropped responders produce actual refusal counters and no invented receiver reads.",
    "C11 retains known initial renewal plus unknown bind commitment, selected-child destruction and closed generic receipt. C12 preserves the two source-prescribed SM record/checkpoint histories, empty bind membership/NotRequired, two refused sends with cached output, and the source-less ACK without settling the SM FIFO.",
    "Deep or malformed supplied XML retains an explicit finding. Truthful unsafe facts remain decodable, and normative Safety precedes fixture comparison. This remains the controlled seam; full HTTP dispatch/auth publication and live SQL are outside the claim."
  ],
